Honor TRIGGERED_IGNORE_EQUIPPED_ITEM_REQUIREMENT in CheckItems' weapon checks.

Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp

Why: bug reports #28/#42/#90 -- "still not seeing garrote or ambush cast
when i use hemorrhage" / "Shadowstep aoe pickpocket doesn't appear to
work" / pickpocket redesign request. Log forensics on Server.log found
~532,000 failed Ambush casts from Living Gear's Hemorrhage spread, all
with SPELL_FAILED_EQUIPPED_ITEM_CLASS_MAINHAND.

The module casts Ambush with TRIGGERED_IGNORE_EQUIPPED_ITEM_REQUIREMENT
(0x00080000) specifically to waive Ambush's dagger requirement, because a
"spread an Ambush" perk cannot sensibly require the rogue to carry a
dagger when Hemorrhage itself takes axes, maces, swords, staves and fists.
But the guard at the top of the weapon-presence block in Spell::CheckItems
had the flag check commented out:

    if (/*never skip those checks !HasTriggeredCastFlag(...) &&*/ ...)

so the flag was a no-op for the ATTR3_REQUIRES_MAIN_HAND_WEAPON /
REQUIRES_OFF_HAND_WEAPON presence-and-fit checks. Every Ambush landed
result 30 and was silently swallowed by TRIGGERED_DONT_REPORT_CAST_ERROR.

The fix re-enables the guard. The flag sits OUTSIDE TRIGGERED_FULL_MASK,
so it is only ever set by explicitly-flagged triggered casts; ordinary
player casts of Ambush still demand the dagger exactly as before.

Secondary module-side fix (mod-living-gear, not this patch): the same log
showed ~115k OUT_OF_RANGE / UNIT_NOT_INFRONT Garrote+Ambush failures
because the spread cast melee-range spells at targets up to 15 yards away
and behind the player, plus ~1.7k BAD_TARGETS on skeletons that cannot
bleed. The spread now gates to melee range + front arc + bleedable
creature types.
